<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">New Republic (Brazil)</h1><p class="st-meta">1985 CE – present · capital Brasília</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Brazil's current democratic era, founded in 1985 after military rule, with a citizens' constitution, the Real Plan and fiercely contested politics.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The end of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/brazilian-military-dictatorship">Brazilian military dictatorship</a> came when an electoral college chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tancredo-neves">Tancredo Neves</a> as president in January 1985. Neves fell ill and died before taking office, and his vice-president, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-sarney">José Sarney</a>, became the first civilian president in 21 years.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Citizen Constitution of 1988 guaranteed broad rights and direct elections. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-collor-de-mello">Fernando Collor</a>, the first directly elected president, resigned during impeachment in 1992. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-henrique-cardoso">Fernando Henrique Cardoso's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/real-plan">Real Plan</a> of 1994 ended hyperinflation. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva">Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva</a>, president from 2003 to 2010, expanded social programmes such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsa-familia">Bolsa Família</a>. His successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilma-rousseff">Dilma Rousseff</a> was impeached in 2016 amid recession and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/operation-car-wash">Car Wash</a> corruption investigation.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jair-bolsonaro">Jair Bolsonaro</a> governed from 2019 to 2022 and lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva">Lula</a>; Bolsonaro's supporters stormed government buildings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brasilia">Brasília</a> on 8 January 2023. In 2025 the Supreme Court convicted Bolsonaro of plotting a coup. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America's</a> largest democracy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/new-republic-brazil.jpg" alt="New Republic (Brazil)" width="320" height="490"><figcaption>Image: Senado Federal · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diretas_J%C3%A1_(4987732126).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1985 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brasília</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Fernando Henrique Cardoso, Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, Jair Bolsonaro</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism, Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/brazil">Brazil</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sixth Brazilian Republic, Federative Republic of Brazil, Brazil</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2006&amp;focus=new-republic-brazil" aria-label="New Republic (Brazil) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3374 2765 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where New Republic (Brazil) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3694 3021L3694 3021"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3694 3021h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3694 3021h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3694 3021h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Brasília. <a href="/atlas?year=2006&amp;focus=new-republic-brazil">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
